{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_013zsrWgQAkfn6oULpszza1c","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Project State Summary\n\n**Problem:** GNU coreutils/moreutils have no formal specs. Go reimplementations diverge on edge cases. This project derives specs from C source, generates Go via AI, and verifies with differential testing against Homebrew reference binaries.\n\n**Architecture:** Four-stage pipeline (extract → specify → synthesize → verify). Components: cmd/ (one package per utility), pkg/sys (syscall abstraction), pkg/format (output formatting), pkg/testutils (differential test harness), pkg/hashutil, pkg/sizeparse, pkg/encutil (shared libraries), magefiles/ (build automation, externally scaffolded).\n\n**Current state:** pkg/sys and pkg/testutils are implemented. All other packages and all cmd/ utilities have `codestatus: not started`. All requirements across all SRDs are `status: ready`.\n\n**Current release:** rel00.0 (Batch 0 — foundational infrastructure). Remaining use cases: uc001-magefiles (only cmd/version is a generation target), uc002-format, uc005-hashutil, uc006-sizeparse, uc007-encutil.\n\n## Priority Reasoning\n\nrel00.0 is the earliest incomplete release. Within it, pkg/sizeparse and pkg/encutil have no dependencies on unimplemented packages (only stdlib). pkg/format depends on pkg/sys (done). pkg/hashutil depends on nothing else. I'll start with sizeparse and encutil since they're leaf dependencies — other utilities (du, split, truncate need sizeparse; base32/base64/basenc need encutil).\n\n## Weight Budgets\n\nAssuming default weight=1 for all requirements (weights not provided inline):\n\n- Task 0: srd087 R1.1(1)+R1.2(1)+R1.3(1)+R1.4(1) = 4 ✓\n- Task 1: srd087 R2.1(1)+R2.2(1)+R3.1(1)+R3.2(1) = 4 ✓\n- Task 2: srd088 R1.1(1)+R1.2(1)+R1.3(1)+R2.1(1) = 4 ✓\n- Task 3: srd088 R2.2(1)+R2.3(1)+R3.1(1)+R3.2(1) = 4 ✓\n\n```yaml\n- index: 0\n  title: \"[stitch] pkg/sizeparse: core Parse and suffix table (srd087-sizeparse R1.1-R1.4)\"\n  dependency: -1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/specs/software-requirements/srd087-sizeparse.yaml (full SRD for size parsing)\n      - pkg/sys/sys.go (existing pkg/ package for style reference)\n\n    files:\n      - path: pkg/sizeparse/parse.go\n        action: create\n        note: Parse function, suffix table, ParseOptions struct, ParseWithOptions stub\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: \"Implement the Parse function per srd087-sizeparse R1.1: accept a string containing a non-negative integer with an optional size suffix and return the corresponding int64 byte count\"\n      - id: R2\n        text: \"Implement the suffix lookup table per srd087-sizeparse R1.2: support K, M, G, T, P, E suffixes for powers of 1024 (KiB=1024, MiB=1048576, etc.) and KB, MB, GB, TB, PB, EB for powers of 1000\"\n      - id: R3\n        text: \"Implement case-insensitive suffix matching per srd087-sizeparse R1.3: accept both uppercase and lowercase suffixes (k, m, g, etc.)\"\n      - id: R4\n        text: \"Implement bare integer handling per srd087-sizeparse R1.4: when no suffix is present, return the numeric value as-is (1 byte per unit)\"\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: \"Export Parse with signature: func Parse(s string) (int64, error) -- per the contract in package_contracts\"\n      - id: D2\n        text: \"Export ParseOptions with signature: type ParseOptions struct { AllowSign bool; DefaultUnit int64 } -- per the contract\"\n      - id: D3\n        text: \"Export ParseWithOptions with signature: func ParseWithOptions(s string, opts ParseOptions) (int64, error) -- stub it in this task, implement in the next task\"\n      - id: D4\n        text: \"Package is pkg/sizeparse. Must not import any cmd/ or other pkg/ package -- stdlib only (fmt, strconv, strings)\"\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: \"Parse(\\\"1024\\\") returns 1024, nil\"\n      - id: AC2\n        text: \"Parse(\\\"1K\\\") returns 1024, nil\"\n      - id: AC3\n        text: \"Parse(\\\"1KB\\\") returns 1000, nil\"\n      - id: AC4\n        text: \"Parse(\\\"1k\\\") returns 1024, nil (case-insensitive)\"\n      - id: AC5\n        text: \"go build ./pkg/sizeparse/... compiles without errors\"\n      - id: AC6\n        text: \"go vet ./pkg/sizeparse/... reports no issues\"\n\n- index: 1\n  title: \"[stitch] pkg/sizeparse: ParseWithOptions and error handling (srd087-sizeparse R2.1-R2.2, R3.1-R3.2)\"\n  dependency: 0\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/specs/software-requirements/srd087-sizeparse.yaml (full SRD for size parsing)\n      - pkg/sizeparse/parse.go (Parse function and suffix table from previous task)\n\n    files:\n      - path: pkg/sizeparse/parse.go\n        action: modify\n        note: Complete ParseWithOptions implementation, add error handling\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: \"Implement ParseWithOptions per srd087-sizeparse R2.1: when AllowSign is true, accept leading + or - signs on the numeric portion and return signed results\"\n      - id: R2\n        text: \"Implement DefaultUnit per srd087-sizeparse R2.2: when DefaultUnit is non-zero and no suffix is present, multiply the bare integer by DefaultUnit instead of treating it as bytes\"\n      - id: R3\n        text: \"Implement error handling per srd087-sizeparse R3.1: return a descriptive error for invalid input (empty string, non-numeric, unknown suffix)\"\n      - id: R4\n        text: \"Implement overflow detection per srd087-sizeparse R3.2: return an error if the computed byte count would overflow int64\"\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: \"ParseWithOptions signature: func ParseWithOptions(s string, opts ParseOptions) (int64, error) -- per the contract\"\n      - id: D2\n        text: \"Parse delegates to ParseWithOptions with zero-value ParseOptions\"\n      - id: D3\n        text: \"Must not import any cmd/ or other pkg/ package\"\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: \"ParseWithOptions(\\\"+1K\\\", ParseOptions{AllowSign: true}) returns 1024, nil\"\n      - id: AC2\n        text: \"ParseWithOptions(\\\"-1K\\\", ParseOptions{AllowSign: true}) returns -1024, nil\"\n      - id: AC3\n        text: \"ParseWithOptions(\\\"1\\\", ParseOptions{DefaultUnit: 512}) returns 512, nil\"\n      - id: AC4\n        text: \"Parse(\\\"\\\") returns 0 and a non-nil error\"\n      - id: AC5\n        text: \"Parse(\\\"999E\\\") handles large values; Parse(\\\"99999999E\\\") returns overflow error\"\n      - id: AC6\n        text: \"go build ./pkg/sizeparse/... compiles without errors\"\n      - id: AC7\n        text: \"go vet ./pkg/sizeparse/... reports no issues\"\n\n- index: 2\n  title: \"[stitch] pkg/encutil: EncoderConfig and Encode (srd088-encutil R1.1-R1.3, R2.1)\"\n  dependency: -1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/specs/software-requirements/srd088-encutil.yaml (full SRD for encoding utilities)\n      - pkg/sys/sys.go (existing pkg/ package for style reference)\n\n    files:\n      - path: pkg/encutil/encode.go\n        action: create\n        note: EncoderConfig, DecoderConfig structs, Encode function, OpenInput function stub\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: \"Implement EncoderConfig per srd088-encutil R1.1: struct with Encode func([]byte) string for the encoding function and WrapCol int for line wrapping column width\"\n      - id: R2\n        text: \"Implement Encode per srd088-encutil R1.2: read all input from r, encode using cfg.Encode, wrap output lines at cfg.WrapCol columns (0 means no wrapping), write to w with a trailing newline\"\n      - id: R3\n        text: \"Implement line wrapping per srd088-encutil R1.3: when WrapCol > 0, insert newlines into the encoded output at every WrapCol characters\"\n      - id: R4\n        text: \"Implement DecoderConfig struct per srd088-encutil R2.1: struct with Decode func(string) ([]byte, error) for the decoding function and IgnoreGarbage bool for skipping invalid characters\"\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: \"Export EncoderConfig with signature: type EncoderConfig struct { Encode func([]byte) string; WrapCol int } -- per the contract\"\n      - id: D2\n        text: \"Export DecoderConfig with signature: type DecoderConfig struct { Decode func(string) ([]byte, error); IgnoreGarbage bool } -- per the contract\"\n      - id: D3\n        text: \"Export Encode with signature: func Encode(r io.Reader, w io.Writer, cfg EncoderConfig) error -- per the contract\"\n      - id: D4\n        text: \"Package is pkg/encutil. Must not import any cmd/ or other pkg/ package -- use io, os, bufio, strings only\"\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: \"Encode reads from an io.Reader, encodes via cfg.Encode, and writes wrapped output to an io.Writer\"\n      - id: AC2\n        text: \"When WrapCol is 76, output lines are at most 76 characters wide\"\n      - id: AC3\n        text: \"When WrapCol is 0, output is a single unwrapped line\"\n      - id: AC4\n        text: \"DecoderConfig struct is exported with Decode and IgnoreGarbage fields\"\n      - id: AC5\n        text: \"go build ./pkg/encutil/... compiles without errors\"\n      - id: AC6\n        text: \"go vet ./pkg/encutil/... reports no issues\"\n\n- index: 3\n  title: \"[stitch] pkg/encutil: Decode and OpenInput (srd088-encutil R2.2-R2.3, R3.1-R3.2)\"\n  dependency: 2\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/specs/software-requirements/srd088-encutil.yaml (full SRD for encoding utilities)\n      - pkg/encutil/encode.go (EncoderConfig, DecoderConfig, Encode from previous task)\n\n    files:\n      - path: pkg/encutil/encode.go\n        action: modify\n        note: Add Decode function and OpenInput function\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: \"Implement Decode per srd088-encutil R2.2: read encoded input from r, strip whitespace, decode using cfg.Decode, and write raw bytes to w\"\n      - id: R2\n        text: \"Implement IgnoreGarbage per srd088-encutil R2.3: when cfg.IgnoreGarbage is true, strip non-alphabet characters from input before decoding instead of returning an error\"\n      - id: R3\n        text: \"Implement OpenInput per srd088-encutil R3.1: when filename is \\\"-\\\" or empty, return os.Stdin; otherwise open the file for reading and return it\"\n      - id: R4\n        text: \"Implement input error handling per srd088-encutil R3.2: return a descriptive error if the file cannot be opened\"\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: \"Export Decode with signature: func Decode(r io.Reader, w io.Writer, cfg DecoderConfig) error -- per the contract\"\n      - id: D2\n        text: \"Export OpenInput with signature: func OpenInput(filename string) (io.ReadCloser, error) -- per the contract\"\n      - id: D3\n        text: \"Must not import any cmd/ or other pkg/ package\"\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: \"Decode reads encoded text from r, decodes via cfg.Decode, and writes binary output to w\"\n      - id: AC2\n        text: \"Decode with IgnoreGarbage=true strips non-alphabet characters before decoding\"\n      - id: AC3\n        text: \"Decode with IgnoreGarbage=false returns an error on invalid input characters\"\n      - id: AC4\n        text: \"OpenInput(\\\"-\\\") returns os.Stdin\"\n      - id: AC5\n        text: \"OpenInput(\\\"nonexistent\\\") returns a non-nil error\"\n      - id: AC6\n        text: \"go build ./pkg/encutil/... compiles without errors\"\n      - id: AC7\n        text: \"go vet ./pkg/encutil/... reports no issues\"\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":60366,"cache_read_input_tokens":11311,"cache_creation":{